WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.828
Part four: reading the pressure–pressure diagram.

00:00:03.978 --> 00:00:14.354
Across: ambient pressure, from 1 bar at the surface, the grey line, to 5 bar at 40 m. Up: nitrogen in one compartment.

00:00:14.504 --> 00:00:25.258
The dot is compartment 1, half-time 5 min, with 0.75 bar of nitrogen. Above the blue line, tissue is supersaturated.

00:00:25.408 --> 00:00:35.136
Descend and stay 20 min: the dot jumps right, then climbs as the tissue takes up nitrogen; the faint line is its path.

00:00:35.286 --> 00:00:45.589
The dotted line is the M-value, the compartment's limit. GF Low allows 30 % of the gap between it and the blue line, GF High 70 %.

00:00:45.739 --> 00:00:55.966
The solid line is the ascent limit: GF Low at the orange anchor, the 18 m first stop, rising to GF High at the surface.

00:00:56.116 --> 00:01:05.519
At the first stop, compartment 2's dot would meet its solid line first if you ascended: it is the controlling compartment, outlined in the selector.

00:01:05.669 --> 00:01:15.471
Later on the last stop, the slower compartment 5 takes over: to surface, its dot must drop below the solid line's left end.

00:01:15.621 --> 00:01:22.149
Surfaced: the dot is above the blue line, supersaturated, but just under the limit you chose.

00:01:22.299 --> 00:01:31.528
One compartment is shown; the plan respects all sixteen. A model, not a guarantee against decompression sickness.

00:01:31.678 --> 00:01:36.537
Try it yourself in the Deco Theory sandbox. Thanks for watching!
